  "title": "A-long Large-Cap Cash-Conversion Preregistration",
  "description": "Research-only preregistration for a diagnostic-derived single-factor cash_conversion hypothesis in the reviewed A-share large-cap top-500 universe, after the large-cap pure-quality composite was falsified but cash_conversion was its strongest single-factor diagnostic. It freezes one cash_conversion primary cell, a two-tier verdict (statistical alpha clue vs tradeable candidate via a rolling relative-NAV drawdown gate), a sub-period robustness gate, and a singleton test-budget boundary. It reuses already-reviewed materialized/audited data, fetches nothing, runs no signal search, authorizes no production use, and proves no alpha.",
